      "writtenOn": "2022-10-13T22:42:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there\u0027s a lot of value in `rc`. In our use case, I mostly expect this to be called from other `libc` functions such as `abort()` and not someone calling `exit(5)`. Generally, I [don\u0027t think exit codes are standardized on Linux](https://stackoverflow.com/q/1101957), so I\u0027m not sure the number would be that meaningful except for zero (success) vs non-zero (failure).\n\nIn the case of `abort()`, [newlib calls `_exit(1)`](https://sourceware.org/git/?p\u003dnewlib-cygwin.git;a\u003dblob;f\u003dnewlib/libc/stdlib/abort.c;h\u003d065dee5b6c710102420d91139434e5fd0897838a;hb\u003d0b6342c97f08765e9873b3c52d61657c2aa596e5#l59).",
